      "message": "Hi Ulya, I realized that I did need to be able to exclude shared libraries from being implicitly added to the manifest in the end. While I could avoid some dependencies that caused that I could not avoid them all.\n\nThis is a quick hack to test the approach (and it works). Would you mind taking a quick look to see if it looks reasonable before I spend the time cleaning it up and adding some tests.\n\nI know that I am modifying in places ClassLoaderContext objects that could be shared across multiple modules which could be a potential source of nasty bugs so that is something that I will need to rectify by copying the objects.\n\nOne slight nastiness was that I had to call the ExcludeLibs() from with aapt.buildActions() as that adds additional entries to the CLCM which is passed in. So, I have to pass the excludedLibs in alongside the CLCM.",
